{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":263433,"duration_api_ms":317291,"num_turns":33,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"14ea72b7-f9c2-4f17-bd36-a4e6c095eec9","total_cost_usd":1.4375353,"usage":{"input_tokens":3331,"cache_creation_input_tokens":61981,"cache_read_input_tokens":1080015,"output_tokens":8383,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":61981,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3331,"outputTokens":8383,"cacheReadInputTokens":1080015,"cacheCreationInputTokens":61981,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.15361875,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1642,"outputTokens":10412,"cacheReadInputTokens":1162283,"cacheCreationInputTokens":91189,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.28391655000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[],"summary":"Reviewed the root-zone oxygenation (ROL) implementation end-to-end: substrate.rs core logic, process.rs parameter definition, engine.rs integration, and all unit/integration tests.\n\n**Correctness:** The saturating exponential formula `depth * (1 - exp(-(biomass * rate) / depth))` correctly preserves linear cm/g slope at low biomass while capping at substrate depth. Guild filtering (`PlantGuild::RootFeedingRosette` only) correctly excludes floating/epiphytic plants. The `root_oxygenation_active_biomass_g` calculation properly weights by habitat_index, substrate_uptake_bias share, and substrate_root_activity_factor.\n\n**Safety:** `rol_rate_cm_per_g` is validated non-negative in invariants. All biomass values are clamped to non-negative. Division by zero is guarded via `f64::MIN_POSITIVE` and early returns when denominators approach epsilon. The effective penetration is clamped to `[0, total_depth]`.\n\n**Integration:** `step_substrate_zones` is called at engine init (line 132) and once per hourly tick (Step 11b, line 410). It recomputes the habitat registry fresh internally via `compute_habitat_registry(state)`, avoiding staleness from the cached `state.habitat_registry`. The returned `SubstrateOxygenationBreakdown` is properly recorded in both tracing notes and budget metrics.\n\n**Serialization:** `rol_rate_cm_per_g` has `#[serde(default)]` with a 0.15 cm/g default, so old save files deserialize correctly. The penetration depth stored on substrate layers is re-derived during engine initialization.\n\n**Test coverage:** All 8 acceptance criteria are met: (1) rooted plants increase penetration vs unplanted, (2) proportional to biomass with diminishing returns, (3) floating plants don't contribute, (4) zero biomass yields zero bonus, (5) named parameter (not hardcoded), (6–7) 500-hour integration tests show divergence in penetration, nitrification, and denitrification, (8) tracing exposes ROL contribution separately. All 28 substrate unit tests and 5 integration tests pass.\n\nNo bugs, safety issues, or correctness gaps found."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"b2423b05-bb49-4ace-bc21-142043e89a52"}
